Source: libsurface
Section: libs
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), git, pkgconf, libdiginet-dev (>= 0.1.2), libmackie-dev (>= 0.1.0)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/FreeMixer/libsurface
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: libsurface0
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: device behaviour of motorised control surfaces
 libsurface is the device behaviour of a motorised control surface, written
 once for every surface and every host: a motor-fader policy that never fights
 the hand, touch with a self-heal and a release debounce, the bank window, a
 shadow of the whole board replayed when a device comes back blank, meter steps
 with hysteresis and LED ring rendering. It speaks no wire and knows no mixing
 semantics.

Package: libsurface-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: libsurface0 (= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Description: device behaviour of motorised control surfaces, development files
 The header and the pkg-config file libsurface, for building a control-surface
 host or backend on libsurface.

Package: libsurface-diginet0
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, libdiginet-transport0 (>= 0.1.2)
Description: Digidesign Control|24 under libsurface, over DigiNet
 libsurface-diginet is libsurface's DigiNet module: a Control|24 driven by
 libsurface's device behaviour over libdiginet's desk mux. One listener hears
 every interface and every desk; each attached desk is a libsurface surface
 whose board is replayed on every new session, and a deaf desk or one owned by
 another host is raised as a warning.

Package: libsurface-diginet-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: libsurface-diginet0 (= ${binary:Version}), libsurface-dev (= ${binary:Version}), libdiginet-dev (>= 0.1.2), ${misc:Depends}
Description: Digidesign Control|24 under libsurface, development files
 The header and the pkg-config file libsurface-diginet, for building a host
 that drives a Control|24 through libsurface.

Package: libsurface-mackie0
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: MCU surface such as the Behringer X-Touch under libsurface
 libsurface-mackie is libsurface's Mackie module: one surface per MCU device,
 the X-Touch's geometry, touch from the touch notes and the host-connection
 handshake, driven by libsurface's device behaviour with libmackie as its codec.
 The MIDI transport stays the host's.

Package: libsurface-mackie-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: libsurface-mackie0 (= ${binary:Version}), libsurface-dev (= ${binary:Version}), libmackie-dev (>= 0.1.0), ${misc:Depends}
Description: MCU surface under libsurface, development files
 The header and the pkg-config file libsurface-mackie, for building a host that
 drives an MCU surface through libsurface.

Package: surface-c24
Section: sound
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, diginet-tools
Description: drive a Control|24 through libsurface, with no privilege of its own
 surface-c24 takes its packet socket from diginet-packet-helper, attaches the
 first Control|24 that announces on any interface, labels its strips, mirrors
 each fader on its meter, prints every event, and takes writes from a FIFO.
